01:21:18,230 --> 01:21:18,970
Check this out.

1369
01:21:19,210 --> 01:21:19,970
We're gonna do that.

1370
01:21:20,870 --> 01:21:21,830
Another observer here.

1371
01:21:22,430 --> 01:21:25,310
Let's say this one is on two, this one is on three.

1372
01:21:30,090 --> 01:21:35,230
Everyone is gonna be wired to a three, because in that case...

1373
01:21:36,620 --> 01:21:37,300
No, no, no.

1374
01:21:37,480 --> 01:21:38,840
They grow at different rates, I guess.

1375
01:21:38,920 --> 01:21:39,320
It's RNG.

1376
01:21:39,780 --> 01:21:49,700
I was gonna say, if this one goes to a 2, and then it waits for this guy to reach 3, then they all activate, similar to how the sugar canes all activate at the same time, right?

1377
01:21:50,740 --> 01:21:51,140
But!

1378
01:21:51,600 --> 01:21:57,400
I didn't think about the fact that these things probably grow differently over time, right?

1379
01:21:59,400 --> 01:22:00,160
Maybe that's okay.

1380
01:22:00,280 --> 01:22:00,840
Maybe I don't care.

1381
01:22:00,980 --> 01:22:01,540
Maybe it's fine.

1382
01:22:02,020 --> 01:22:02,420
Honestly.

1383
01:22:04,300 --> 01:22:04,700
Uh...

1384
01:22:07,120 --> 01:22:09,340
Yeah, I mean, there's going to be a bit of loss.

1385
01:22:09,700 --> 01:22:11,380
You know, it's not perfect efficiency.

1386
01:22:13,960 --> 01:22:14,880
It's fine.

1387
01:22:15,220 --> 01:22:15,760
Am I coping?

1388
01:22:15,940 --> 01:22:16,740
Fuck, I think I'm coping.

1389
01:22:17,240 --> 01:22:17,720
God damn it.

1390
01:22:17,800 --> 01:22:20,540
Let me try and drink properly from my can without spilling all over myself.

1391
01:22:25,120 --> 01:22:25,700
Oh, man.

1392
01:22:25,920 --> 01:22:26,240
Okay.

1393
01:22:29,300 --> 01:22:31,840
Uh... Hmm...

1394
01:22:36,360 --> 01:22:37,200
Wait a minute.

1395
01:22:38,580 --> 01:22:40,920
I'm gonna ask a stupid-ass question now.

1396
01:22:41,740 --> 01:22:43,240
Obviously it's a rhetorical one.

1397
01:22:44,200 --> 01:22:50,920
But... if the farmers are planting this... are they... harvesting it?

1398
01:22:55,700 --> 01:22:56,580
Wait a minute.

1399
01:23:00,080 --> 01:23:01,380
Hold on a minute now.

1400
01:23:03,280 --> 01:23:04,660
I need more bone meal.

1401
01:23:07,550 --> 01:23:08,350
Meal me up.

1402
01:23:12,770 --> 01:23:16,750
Like... Or maybe I have to harvest it and they just grow it.

1403
01:23:22,230 --> 01:23:23,010
Oh, wait.

1404
01:23:24,090 --> 01:23:25,050
Wait, what's this one?

1405
01:23:25,370 --> 01:23:26,250
Oh, it's taters!

1406
01:23:27,330 --> 01:23:28,410
It's taters, precious.

1407
01:23:41,350 --> 01:23:41,870
Okay.

1408
01:23:41,870 --> 01:23:43,750
And we are going to need this guy.

1409
01:23:50,590 --> 01:23:51,110
Okay.

1410
01:23:53,610 --> 01:23:55,570
So now we know everything is grown, right?

1411
01:23:59,520 --> 01:24:00,480
Uh, where's the farmer?

1412
01:24:01,260 --> 01:24:01,980
There you are.

1413
01:24:03,380 --> 01:24:03,960
Ah, wait a minute!

1414
01:24:04,040 --> 01:24:04,800
Are we good now?

1415
01:24:04,900 --> 01:24:05,160
Look!

1416
01:24:05,460 --> 01:24:06,480
We're on good terms!

1417
01:24:07,640 --> 01:24:08,620
They love me now!

1418
01:24:10,460 --> 01:24:10,860
Yeah!

1419
01:24:11,480 --> 01:24:12,160
They love me now!

1420
01:24:13,120 --> 01:24:13,760
Love me!

1421
01:24:13,920 --> 01:24:14,440
Love me!

1422
01:24:15,260 --> 01:24:16,680
Farmer, are you gonna do your thing?

1423
01:24:21,600 --> 01:24:24,720
Can you go down there and maybe, you know, do a bit of harvesting?

1424
01:24:26,160 --> 01:24:27,260
Dude, maybe they need a chest?

1425
01:24:28,160 --> 01:24:29,600
I was like, where are they going to put it?

1426
01:24:30,720 --> 01:24:31,980
Let's put a chest right next to it.

1427
01:24:32,140 --> 01:24:32,640
I want to see.

1428
01:24:35,200 --> 01:24:35,920
Chest, chest, chest.

1429
01:24:36,160 --> 01:24:36,820
Make one for me.

1430
01:24:42,200 --> 01:24:44,280
Maybe they'll know if I put it right next to it, you know?

1431
01:24:47,120 --> 01:24:47,940
There, go nuts.

1432
01:24:50,260 --> 01:24:51,720
Let me remove this one as well.

1433
01:24:53,720 --> 01:24:54,820
Stuart is invisible again.

1434
01:24:54,960 --> 01:24:56,960
Oh man, don't remind me, Stuart.

1435
01:24:57,980 --> 01:25:00,300
Don't remind me about the invisibility potion.

1436
01:25:03,240 --> 01:25:05,080
You know, maybe they're inside because it's raining.

1437
01:25:06,380 --> 01:25:08,400
Oh yeah, look, everyone is sort of... Let's go to bed.

1438
01:25:09,340 --> 01:25:11,720
We're going to wait until the next day and see what happens.

1439
01:25:15,750 --> 01:25:16,550
You see that?

1440
01:25:16,670 --> 01:25:17,750
He drank milk to get out.

1441
01:25:18,010 --> 01:25:18,550
That's funny.

1442
01:25:20,770 --> 01:25:22,410
Yeah, you're a funny man, Stuart.

1443
01:25:25,070 --> 01:25:25,550
Farmer?

1444
01:25:27,610 --> 01:25:28,090
Farmer?

1445
01:25:35,120 --> 01:25:35,840
Where is he?

1446
01:25:36,060 --> 01:25:37,120
Where is that scoundrel?

1447
01:25:39,420 --> 01:25:40,200
There you are.

1448
01:25:41,560 --> 01:25:43,840
I wanna... I wanna... You know what?

1449
01:25:43,900 --> 01:25:45,240
I'm gonna actually just observe you.

1450
01:25:46,100 --> 01:25:47,180
Let's see what you're gonna do.

1451
01:25:49,220 --> 01:25:52,740
Maybe... Okay, maybe he doesn't actually... Let's leave some of these open.

1452
01:25:53,120 --> 01:25:54,380
See if he does something now.

1453
01:25:57,830 --> 01:25:58,490
Come on.

1454
01:25:58,630 --> 01:26:01,110
Don't fraternize with the librarian.

1455
01:26:03,130 --> 01:26:04,270
Don't hide behind him.

1456
01:26:04,910 --> 01:26:05,790
Go to work.

1457
01:26:08,170 --> 01:26:11,150
Or I will bash you upside your head with this note block.

1458
01:26:11,910 --> 01:26:12,930
You want that?

1459
01:26:14,030 --> 01:26:14,550
Huh?

1460
01:26:15,150 --> 01:26:15,670
Go.

1461
01:26:16,010 --> 01:26:16,630
Come on.

1462
01:26:19,190 --> 01:26:25,330
For a second I thought, why build a machine when I have a perfectly well-oiled machine right here by the name of... I don't know.

1463
01:26:25,530 --> 01:26:26,030
Fucking...

1464
01:26:27,520 --> 01:26:28,300
I don't even know.

1465
01:26:29,000 --> 01:26:29,720
Jeremy, you know?

1466
01:26:29,840 --> 01:26:30,020
Whatever.

1467
01:26:30,760 --> 01:26:34,400
This is a machine, and it's an organic machine produced by evolution.

1468
01:26:35,420 --> 01:26:37,200
He will do what I ask of him.

1469
01:26:37,640 --> 01:26:38,460
It's not slavery.

1470
01:26:39,160 --> 01:26:41,420
It's just me asking for a favor, and he does it.

1471
01:26:42,580 --> 01:26:43,380
Go to work!

1472
01:26:45,040 --> 01:26:45,580
Come on!

1473
01:26:49,600 --> 01:26:50,080
Motherfucker.

1474
01:26:50,260 --> 01:26:50,360
Okay.

1475
01:26:50,740 --> 01:26:51,780
Maybe he doesn't do that, actually.

1476
01:26:52,740 --> 01:26:54,500
I gotta do everything myself, huh?

1477
01:26:55,500 --> 01:26:56,920
But he definitely plants.

1478
01:26:56,980 --> 01:26:57,700
We saw that.

1479
01:27:45,490 --> 01:27:46,270
Where is it?

1480
01:27:46,670 --> 01:27:47,530
He broke it.

1481
01:27:53,010 --> 01:27:54,330
Is it somewhere here?

1482
01:28:00,750 --> 01:28:01,270
Huh.

1483
01:28:02,890 --> 01:28:05,590
He definitely took it, because it's not on the ground.

1484
01:28:12,190 --> 01:28:12,910
Break something more.

1485
01:28:13,010 --> 01:28:13,270
Break more.

1486
01:28:13,390 --> 01:28:15,410
Okay, he doesn't want to do it when I'm close.

1487
01:28:20,410 --> 01:28:21,810
He's standing on top of the chest.

1488
01:28:27,870 --> 01:28:29,310
He put something in here now.

1489
01:28:30,470 --> 01:28:31,430
Oh, look, look, look, look!

1490
01:28:38,040 --> 01:28:39,280
Where is he taking it?

1491
01:28:40,660 --> 01:28:41,620
He's farming!

1492
01:28:48,400 --> 01:28:49,620
Where are you taking it?

1493
01:28:50,380 --> 01:28:50,900
Look!

1494
01:28:51,120 --> 01:28:53,280
You can see him picking it up too.

1495
01:29:09,410 --> 01:29:10,550
He's taking them all.

1496
01:29:17,370 --> 01:29:18,130
Yeah, yeah.

1497
01:29:18,610 --> 01:29:21,930
Oh, you know, maybe he needs to pick them all up first, and then he does something with them.

1498
01:29:23,650 --> 01:29:24,550
Let's keep watching.

1499
01:29:32,810 --> 01:29:34,150
That's definitely a farmer.

1500
01:29:53,410 --> 01:29:56,250
Maybe I need to designate a chest to him or something.

1501
01:29:58,670 --> 01:29:59,790
Come on, you're almost done.

1502
01:29:59,910 --> 01:30:00,450
You need two more.

1503
01:30:01,370 --> 01:30:01,810
Crap.

1504
01:30:02,390 --> 01:30:04,750
He puts them in the... in the composter.

1505
01:30:06,530 --> 01:30:06,970
Wait.

1506
01:30:11,810 --> 01:30:16,570
How did... Can I get it out of the composter somehow?

1507
01:30:35,300 --> 01:30:36,480
Okay, okay, here we go, here we go.

1508
01:30:37,740 --> 01:30:38,380
What are you gonna do?

1509
01:30:43,300 --> 01:30:44,580
Okay, he took them all now.

1510
01:30:45,540 --> 01:30:47,480
How come he's not planting these, by the way?

1511
01:30:48,200 --> 01:30:50,980
Oh, maybe they're not directly connected to the water.

1512
01:30:56,300 --> 01:30:57,020
Oh, you know what?

1513
01:30:57,020 --> 01:30:59,740
He's standing on top of the chest because he wants to get to this one.

1514
01:30:59,940 --> 01:31:00,540
Oh, shit.

1515
01:31:03,630 --> 01:31:04,990
Here, let me make some space for you.

1516
01:31:05,090 --> 01:31:05,710
Maybe that's the issue.

1517
01:31:09,170 --> 01:31:10,310
No, put it in the chest.

1518
01:31:11,590 --> 01:31:13,810
Like, he's picking up all of the wheat.

1519
01:31:20,670 --> 01:31:21,030
Okay.

1520
01:31:24,990 --> 01:31:26,150
I'm gonna keep watching him.

1521
01:31:30,080 --> 01:31:31,520
Tell me that doesn't look like a face.

1522
01:31:32,020 --> 01:31:36,140
Two eyes, nose, or even a mouth, and... I don't know.

1523
01:31:36,500 --> 01:31:37,380
Some kind of mask?

1524
01:31:43,940 --> 01:31:45,560
What happens when the composter is full?

1525
01:31:47,000 --> 01:31:48,140
Let me put something else in there.

1526
01:32:11,720 --> 01:32:12,740
He has an emerald.

1527
01:32:16,900 --> 01:32:17,600
Give it to me.

1528
01:32:18,920 --> 01:32:19,540
Give it to me.

1529
01:32:22,320 --> 01:32:22,860
It's mine.

1530
01:32:24,720 --> 01:32:25,740
What are you gonna do with it?

1531
01:32:36,390 --> 01:32:38,030
Where's the... where's the money?

1532
01:32:38,810 --> 01:32:40,050
He pocketed it!

1533
01:32:40,910 --> 01:32:46,070
It's like that guy from Blood Diamond, who tried to pocket the diamond in between his toes.

1534
01:32:46,930 --> 01:32:48,030
I saw that!

1535
01:32:48,770 --> 01:32:49,610
Hand it over.

1536
01:32:51,410 --> 01:32:52,210
Hand it over.

1537
01:32:56,150 --> 01:32:57,090
Oh my god.

1538
01:32:59,530 --> 01:33:03,170
What happened to the... Did he give it to me?

1539
01:33:04,010 --> 01:33:04,790
No, he didn't.

1540
01:33:06,270 --> 01:33:08,050
Now he's acting as if nothing happened.

1541
01:33:10,790 --> 01:33:12,110
I saw you, motherfucker.

1542
01:33:12,330 --> 01:33:12,930
I saw what you did.

1543
01:33:15,330 --> 01:33:16,390
Where did you get that money?

1544
01:33:19,310 --> 01:33:20,330
This is a mystery?

1545
01:33:21,570 --> 01:33:22,850
Okay, you know what we're gonna do?

1546
01:33:26,650 --> 01:33:28,310
Uh... Huh.

1547
01:33:28,870 --> 01:33:29,230
Hmm.

1548
01:33:29,890 --> 01:33:30,230
Wait.

1549
01:33:33,730 --> 01:33:36,330
He had the emerald when he saw this, didn't he?

1550
01:33:38,710 --> 01:33:40,130
Oh, he picked it up!

1551
01:33:48,660 --> 01:33:50,020
Wait, did I pick it up or did he?

1552
01:33:53,100 --> 01:33:53,420
Look!

1553
01:33:56,260 --> 01:33:57,200
He's taking it!

1554
01:34:11,580 --> 01:34:13,280
Well, great, now he took all of it.

1555
01:34:13,300 --> 01:34:13,720
What now?

1556
01:34:20,020 --> 01:34:22,240
I'm so confused right now.

1557
01:34:25,300 --> 01:34:25,820
Huh?

1558
01:34:27,900 --> 01:34:29,960
This is the biggest mystery yet.

1559
01:34:31,800 --> 01:34:34,080
Well, maybe not the biggest, but it's definitely up there.

1560
01:34:35,660 --> 01:34:37,400
You know something, don't you?

1561
01:34:41,700 --> 01:34:43,060
Maybe there's like a threshold.

1562
01:34:43,380 --> 01:34:43,760
Do you need more?

1563
01:34:47,180 --> 01:34:49,620
Okay, so they can actually pick things up.

1564
01:34:51,560 --> 01:34:52,760
What about wheat?

1565
01:34:52,920 --> 01:34:53,400
Do you like this?

1566
01:34:54,160 --> 01:34:54,800
Hey!

1567
01:35:03,900 --> 01:35:04,580
Yes!

1568
01:35:05,740 --> 01:35:07,940
Am I just giving away all my shit?

1569
01:35:08,740 --> 01:35:09,160
Wait!

1570
01:35:10,120 --> 01:35:12,040
I'm just giving everything away!

1571
01:35:13,160 --> 01:35:14,180
Oh no!

1572
01:35:17,870 --> 01:35:19,110
Wait a minute, what else can I give him?

1573
01:35:21,670 --> 01:35:22,650
Farming stuff, I imagine.

1574
01:35:22,790 --> 01:35:25,610
What about some bamboo... fucking everything?

1575
01:35:28,290 --> 01:35:29,510
Put some of the stuff back in here.

1576
01:35:33,910 --> 01:35:35,350
Oh, wait, is it becoming night?

1577
01:35:36,530 --> 01:35:38,150
Okay, I guess I'll go to sleep as well.

1578
01:35:38,430 --> 01:35:39,830
Why are they asleep so early?

1579
01:35:40,010 --> 01:35:40,490
There we go.

1580
01:35:45,660 --> 01:35:46,280
Okay, let's go.

1581
01:35:48,920 --> 01:35:51,140
You know you want to go to... No, you don't want to go to work, it seems.

1582
01:35:51,240 --> 01:35:51,340
Here.

1583
01:35:54,780 --> 01:35:55,720
You're going to pick that up, too?

1584
01:36:02,860 --> 01:36:03,320
Come on.

1585
01:36:03,600 --> 01:36:04,520
You don't want that, huh?

1586
01:36:08,140 --> 01:36:09,220
He doesn't want these.

1587
01:36:09,440 --> 01:36:09,640
Okay.

1588
01:36:11,140 --> 01:36:11,700
Malon seats.

1589
01:36:20,840 --> 01:36:22,240
No.

1590
01:36:22,240 --> 01:36:23,640
Bamboo?

1591
01:36:32,480 --> 01:36:33,080
Nope.

1592
01:36:35,100 --> 01:36:36,360
You want this, don't you?

1593
01:36:37,560 --> 01:36:39,420
Like, he wants that so bad!

1594
01:36:39,640 --> 01:36:41,540
He's dreaming about bone meal!

1595
01:36:43,800 --> 01:36:45,800
That's all his mind centers around.

1596
01:36:46,880 --> 01:36:48,180
Wheat seeds as well, right?

1597
01:36:50,820 --> 01:36:51,760
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

1598
01:36:54,140 --> 01:36:55,480
He likes those.

1599
01:36:56,980 --> 01:36:57,580
Taters?

1600
01:37:03,100 --> 01:37:03,540
Okay.

1601
01:37:04,840 --> 01:37:05,760
Raw taters.

1602
01:37:06,020 --> 01:37:06,480
Go plant them.

1603
01:37:08,380 --> 01:37:09,300
Oh, he took it!

1604
01:37:10,320 --> 01:37:13,940
Okay, so maybe I can teach him what to plant.

1605
01:37:14,420 --> 01:37:19,460
Instead of him planting wheat all the time, I can be like, now you are a potato man.

1606
01:37:20,300 --> 01:37:20,880
You know?

1607
01:37:24,480 --> 01:37:25,360
Plant potatoes!

1608
01:37:25,780 --> 01:37:26,220
Taters!

1609
01:37:29,100 --> 01:37:29,620
Wait.

1610
01:37:31,020 --> 01:37:32,200
It wasn't for you!

1611
01:37:32,760 --> 01:37:33,860
He took it!

1612
01:37:34,180 --> 01:37:35,420
It wasn't even for it!

1613
01:37:35,700 --> 01:37:36,000
Oh.

1614
01:37:36,860 --> 01:37:37,660
You want taters?

1615
01:37:41,300 --> 01:37:43,620
Why am I able to give them items, actually?

1616
01:37:43,620 --> 01:37:44,600
This is so confusing.

1617
01:37:45,320 --> 01:37:46,380
What else do I have?

1618
01:37:49,160 --> 01:37:50,440
What about some fish?

1619
01:37:51,680 --> 01:37:52,800
Maybe more wheat?

1620
01:37:54,180 --> 01:37:54,700
Apples?

1621
01:38:04,000 --> 01:38:05,700
You don't like that, do you?

1622
01:38:13,300 --> 01:38:14,320
Come on.

1623
01:38:17,000 --> 01:38:17,840
No?

1624
01:38:19,220 --> 01:38:20,060
Hmm.

1625
01:38:22,020 --> 01:38:23,200
Very weird.

1626
01:38:23,700 --> 01:38:24,580
Do you like apples?

1627
01:38:26,000 --> 01:38:27,040
Farmer man.

1628
01:38:30,560 --> 01:38:31,240
Yo, wait a minute.

1629
01:38:31,320 --> 01:38:33,300
I'm starting to think maybe it's not even farmer-related.

1630
01:38:34,620 --> 01:38:35,920
Can I give bone meal to the others?

1631
01:38:36,020 --> 01:38:36,340
Let's check.

1632
01:38:43,400 --> 01:38:45,160
Okay, maybe it is farmer-related.

1633
01:38:46,160 --> 01:38:47,380
On the bone meal, at least.

1634
01:38:49,400 --> 01:38:49,940
Hey, you there!

1635
01:38:56,840 --> 01:38:58,260
Nope, they're not taking it.

1636
01:38:58,440 --> 01:39:02,760
Okay, so there are specific ones you can only give to the farmer.

1637
01:39:05,640 --> 01:39:06,860
Look, he's farming now.

1638
01:39:11,000 --> 01:39:11,400
